note.text:
Solid–solid mixtures are separated by using a difference between the two solids:
• hand-picking: big pieces of different colour (stones from rice or beans);
• sieving: different sizes (garri, sand and gravel);
• magnetic separation: one solid is attracted by a magnet (iron filings from sand);
• winnowing: one part is much lighter (chaff from rice, maize or beans);
• sublimation: one solid sublimes on heating (iodine or ammonium chloride from sand or salt);
• dissolving, filtering and evaporating: one solid dissolves in water and the other does not (salt from sand).
